{"website":{"seo":{"siteTitle":"","metaDescription":"","defaultKeywords":[],"canonicalBase":"","ogImage":"","twitterHandle":"","googleSiteVerification":"","bingSiteVerification":"","googleAnalyticsId":"","googleTagManagerId":""},"technical":{"robotsTxt":"User-agent: *\nAllow: \/","htaccess":"","blogPath":"\/blog","includeBlogsInSitemap":true},"_id":"6abd61264798ced72885fea2","name":"besttraveladvisory","domain":"besttraveladvisory.com","description":"","platform":"coded","active":true,"faviconUrl":"","createdAt":"2026-09-30T19:21:10.642Z","__v":0},"blog":{"cta":{"label":"Get Quote","url":"\/contact"},"_id":"6ac1ee6201767108a445dca6","websiteId":"6abd61264798ced72885fea2","title":"20 Cheapest Countries to Visit for Budget Travelers","slug":"cheapest-countries-to-visit","content":"<p>Every&nbsp;traveler&nbsp;has&nbsp;felt&nbsp;it&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;that&nbsp;itch&nbsp;to&nbsp;explore&nbsp;somewhere&nbsp;new,&nbsp;held&nbsp;back&nbsp;only&nbsp;by&nbsp;the&nbsp;fear&nbsp;of&nbsp;an&nbsp;empty&nbsp;bank&nbsp;account.&nbsp;The&nbsp;good&nbsp;news?&nbsp;A&nbsp;tight&nbsp;budget&nbsp;doesn&#39;t&nbsp;have&nbsp;to&nbsp;mean&nbsp;staying&nbsp;home.&nbsp;There&nbsp;are&nbsp;dozens&nbsp;of&nbsp;destinations&nbsp;around&nbsp;the&nbsp;world&nbsp;where&nbsp;your&nbsp;money&nbsp;stretches&nbsp;so&nbsp;far,&nbsp;you&#39;ll&nbsp;wonder&nbsp;why&nbsp;you&nbsp;ever&nbsp;spent&nbsp;a&nbsp;fortune&nbsp;elsewhere.<\/p><p><\/p><p>Whether&nbsp;you&#39;re&nbsp;a&nbsp;first-time&nbsp;backpacker&nbsp;or&nbsp;a&nbsp;seasoned&nbsp;explorer&nbsp;looking&nbsp;to&nbsp;cut&nbsp;costs&nbsp;without&nbsp;cutting&nbsp;experiences,&nbsp;this&nbsp;guide&nbsp;is&nbsp;for&nbsp;you.&nbsp;We&#39;ve&nbsp;rounded&nbsp;up&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>20&nbsp;cheapest&nbsp;countries&nbsp;to&nbsp;visit<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;covering&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;food,&nbsp;hotels,&nbsp;transport,&nbsp;and&nbsp;top&nbsp;attractions&nbsp;for&nbsp;each&nbsp;one.&nbsp;From&nbsp;the&nbsp;temples&nbsp;of&nbsp;Southeast&nbsp;Asia&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;beaches&nbsp;of&nbsp;Latin&nbsp;America,&nbsp;<strong><u><a href=\"https:\/\/yoyoguide.com\/best-budget-travel-destinations-for-families-in-2026-guide\/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">budget&nbsp;travel&nbsp;destinations<\/a><\/u><\/strong>&nbsp;have&nbsp;never&nbsp;looked&nbsp;this&nbsp;good.<\/p><p><\/p><p>If&nbsp;you&#39;re&nbsp;also&nbsp;planning&nbsp;and&nbsp;want&nbsp;tips&nbsp;on&nbsp;stretching&nbsp;every&nbsp;dollar&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;road,&nbsp;check&nbsp;out&nbsp;our&nbsp;guide&nbsp;on&nbsp;<strong>How&nbsp;to&nbsp;Travel&nbsp;the&nbsp;World&nbsp;on&nbsp;a&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;Without&nbsp;Missing&nbsp;the&nbsp;Best&nbsp;Experiences<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>1.&nbsp;Thailand<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$30\u2013$50<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Thailand&nbsp;remains&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;beloved&nbsp;<strong>cheap&nbsp;countries&nbsp;to&nbsp;travel<\/strong>&nbsp;to,&nbsp;and&nbsp;for&nbsp;good&nbsp;reason.&nbsp;<strong>Street&nbsp;food<\/strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;everywhere&nbsp;and&nbsp;incredibly&nbsp;cheap&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;a&nbsp;bowl&nbsp;of&nbsp;pad&nbsp;thai&nbsp;or&nbsp;a&nbsp;plate&nbsp;of&nbsp;fried&nbsp;rice&nbsp;costs&nbsp;as&nbsp;little&nbsp;as&nbsp;<strong>$1\u2013$2<\/strong>&nbsp;at&nbsp;local&nbsp;markets&nbsp;and&nbsp;roadside&nbsp;stalls.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;guesthouses&nbsp;and&nbsp;hostels&nbsp;in&nbsp;cities&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>Chiang&nbsp;Mai<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Bangkok<\/strong>&nbsp;range&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$8\u2013$15&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;while&nbsp;mid-range&nbsp;hotels&nbsp;hover&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$25\u2013$40<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p>Getting&nbsp;around&nbsp;is&nbsp;a&nbsp;breeze.&nbsp;<strong>Tuk-tuks,&nbsp;songthaews<\/strong>&nbsp;(shared&nbsp;taxis),&nbsp;and&nbsp;local&nbsp;buses&nbsp;keep&nbsp;transport&nbsp;costs&nbsp;between&nbsp;<strong>$1\u2013$5<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;trip.&nbsp;For&nbsp;longer&nbsp;distances,&nbsp;overnight&nbsp;trains&nbsp;and&nbsp;buses&nbsp;are&nbsp;both&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;and&nbsp;comfortable.&nbsp;Top&nbsp;attractions&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>Wat&nbsp;Pho<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Grand&nbsp;Palace<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;stunning&nbsp;islands&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Koh&nbsp;Samui<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Koh&nbsp;Lanta<\/strong>&nbsp;make&nbsp;Thailand&nbsp;a&nbsp;bucket-list&nbsp;destination&nbsp;that&nbsp;won&#39;t&nbsp;drain&nbsp;your&nbsp;wallet.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>2.&nbsp;Vietnam<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$25\u2013$40<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Vietnam&nbsp;is&nbsp;a&nbsp;dream&nbsp;for&nbsp;<strong>low-cost&nbsp;travel&nbsp;destinations<\/strong>&nbsp;seekers.&nbsp;You&nbsp;can&nbsp;eat&nbsp;like&nbsp;royalty&nbsp;on&nbsp;almost&nbsp;nothing&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;a&nbsp;steaming&nbsp;bowl&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>pho<\/strong>&nbsp;from&nbsp;a&nbsp;street&nbsp;vendor&nbsp;costs&nbsp;as&nbsp;little&nbsp;as&nbsp;<strong>$1<\/strong>,&nbsp;while&nbsp;a&nbsp;full&nbsp;meal&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;local&nbsp;restaurant&nbsp;rarely&nbsp;exceeds&nbsp;<strong>$3\u2013$5<\/strong>.&nbsp;Hostels&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Hanoi<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Ho&nbsp;Chi&nbsp;Minh&nbsp;City<\/strong>&nbsp;start&nbsp;from&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$10&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;budget&nbsp;hotels&nbsp;are&nbsp;widely&nbsp;available&nbsp;for&nbsp;<strong>$15\u2013$25<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p>Local&nbsp;transport&nbsp;is&nbsp;equally&nbsp;wallet-friendly.&nbsp;Sleeper&nbsp;buses&nbsp;and&nbsp;trains&nbsp;connecting&nbsp;cities&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>Hue<\/strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Hoi&nbsp;An<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Da&nbsp;Nang<\/strong>&nbsp;cost&nbsp;between&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$20<\/strong>.&nbsp;Renting&nbsp;a&nbsp;<strong>motorbike<\/strong>&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;day&nbsp;runs&nbsp;about&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$8<\/strong>,&nbsp;making&nbsp;it&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;popular&nbsp;way&nbsp;to&nbsp;explore.&nbsp;Don&#39;t&nbsp;miss&nbsp;<strong>Halong&nbsp;Bay<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;ancient&nbsp;town&nbsp;of&nbsp;Hoi&nbsp;An,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;terraced&nbsp;rice&nbsp;fields&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Sapa<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>3.&nbsp;Indonesia<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$30\u2013$50<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Indonesia,&nbsp;particularly&nbsp;<strong>Bali<\/strong>,&nbsp;is&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;sought-after&nbsp;yet&nbsp;surprisingly&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;destinations&nbsp;in&nbsp;Asia.&nbsp;<strong>Warungs<\/strong>&nbsp;(local&nbsp;eateries)&nbsp;serve&nbsp;generous&nbsp;portions&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>nasi&nbsp;goreng<\/strong>&nbsp;(fried&nbsp;rice)&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>mie&nbsp;goreng<\/strong>&nbsp;(fried&nbsp;noodles)&nbsp;for&nbsp;as&nbsp;little&nbsp;as&nbsp;<strong>$1\u2013$3<\/strong>.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;guesthouses&nbsp;and&nbsp;homestays&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Ubud<\/strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>Canggu<\/strong>&nbsp;range&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$20&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Scooter&nbsp;rentals<\/strong>&nbsp;at&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$8&nbsp;per&nbsp;day<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the&nbsp;go-to&nbsp;way&nbsp;to&nbsp;get&nbsp;around&nbsp;the&nbsp;island.&nbsp;For&nbsp;inter-island&nbsp;travel,&nbsp;<strong>ferries<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;budget-friendly&nbsp;option.&nbsp;Explore&nbsp;the&nbsp;iconic&nbsp;<strong>Tegalalang&nbsp;Rice&nbsp;Terraces<\/strong>,&nbsp;hike&nbsp;<strong>Mount&nbsp;Batur<\/strong>,&nbsp;surf&nbsp;the&nbsp;waves&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>Kuta<\/strong>,&nbsp;or&nbsp;visit&nbsp;the&nbsp;ancient&nbsp;temple&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Prambanan<\/strong>&nbsp;in&nbsp;Java&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;all&nbsp;without&nbsp;spending&nbsp;a&nbsp;fortune.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>4.&nbsp;Cambodia<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$25\u2013$40<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Cambodia&nbsp;is&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>cheapest&nbsp;places&nbsp;to&nbsp;travel<\/strong>&nbsp;in&nbsp;Southeast&nbsp;Asia,&nbsp;especially&nbsp;for&nbsp;first-time&nbsp;budget&nbsp;travelers.&nbsp;<strong>Street&nbsp;food<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;local&nbsp;restaurants&nbsp;serve&nbsp;filling&nbsp;meals&nbsp;for&nbsp;<strong>$1\u2013$3<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;draft&nbsp;beers&nbsp;are&nbsp;famously&nbsp;cheap&nbsp;at&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$0.50<\/strong>.&nbsp;Hostel&nbsp;dorms&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Phnom&nbsp;Penh<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Siem&nbsp;Reap<\/strong>&nbsp;go&nbsp;for&nbsp;as&nbsp;little&nbsp;as&nbsp;<strong>$4\u2013$8&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;with&nbsp;private&nbsp;rooms&nbsp;available&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$20<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Tuk-tuks<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the&nbsp;primary&nbsp;mode&nbsp;of&nbsp;transport&nbsp;and&nbsp;cost&nbsp;about&nbsp;<strong>$2\u2013$5<\/strong>&nbsp;for&nbsp;short&nbsp;trips.&nbsp;The&nbsp;headline&nbsp;attraction&nbsp;is,&nbsp;of&nbsp;course,&nbsp;the&nbsp;breathtaking&nbsp;<strong>Angkor&nbsp;Wat<\/strong>&nbsp;complex&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;a&nbsp;UNESCO&nbsp;World&nbsp;Heritage&nbsp;Site&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;3-day&nbsp;pass&nbsp;costing&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$62<\/strong>.&nbsp;Other&nbsp;must-sees&nbsp;include&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Killing&nbsp;Fields<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Royal&nbsp;Palace<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;floating&nbsp;villages&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Tonle&nbsp;Sap&nbsp;Lake<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>5.&nbsp;Philippines<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$25\u2013$45<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>The&nbsp;Philippines&nbsp;offers&nbsp;over&nbsp;<strong>7,000&nbsp;islands<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;stunning&nbsp;scenery&nbsp;at&nbsp;surprisingly&nbsp;low&nbsp;prices.&nbsp;Local&nbsp;meals&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>adobo<\/strong>,&nbsp;<strong>sinigang<\/strong>,&nbsp;or&nbsp;<strong>lechon<\/strong>&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>carinderias<\/strong>&nbsp;(local&nbsp;eateries)&nbsp;cost&nbsp;as&nbsp;little&nbsp;as&nbsp;<strong>$1\u2013$2<\/strong>.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;guesthouses&nbsp;in&nbsp;popular&nbsp;areas&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>El&nbsp;Nido<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Boracay<\/strong>&nbsp;start&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$20&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Jeepneys<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>tricycles<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the&nbsp;cheapest&nbsp;way&nbsp;to&nbsp;get&nbsp;around&nbsp;cities,&nbsp;costing&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$0.20\u2013$0.50<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;ride.&nbsp;<strong>Ferries<\/strong>&nbsp;connect&nbsp;the&nbsp;islands&nbsp;affordably,&nbsp;though&nbsp;budget&nbsp;flights&nbsp;via&nbsp;<strong>Cebu&nbsp;Pacific<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;worth&nbsp;checking.&nbsp;Top&nbsp;draws&nbsp;include&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Chocolate&nbsp;Hills<\/strong>&nbsp;of&nbsp;Bohol,&nbsp;the&nbsp;pristine&nbsp;beaches&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Palawan<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;world-class&nbsp;diving&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Tubbataha&nbsp;Reef<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>6.&nbsp;India<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$20\u2013$35<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>India&nbsp;is&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;<strong><u><a href=\"https:\/\/besttraveladvisory.com\/budget-international-travel-guide-for-indians\/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">affordable&nbsp;countries&nbsp;to&nbsp;visit<\/a><\/u><\/strong>&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;planet,&nbsp;particularly&nbsp;when&nbsp;it&nbsp;comes&nbsp;to&nbsp;food.&nbsp;A&nbsp;<strong>thali<\/strong>&nbsp;(full&nbsp;meal&nbsp;with&nbsp;curries,&nbsp;rice,&nbsp;and&nbsp;bread)&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;local&nbsp;dhaba&nbsp;costs&nbsp;as&nbsp;little&nbsp;as&nbsp;<strong>$1\u2013$2<\/strong>.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;guesthouses&nbsp;across&nbsp;cities&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>Jaipur<\/strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Varanasi<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Goa<\/strong>&nbsp;start&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$15&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p>India&#39;s&nbsp;extensive&nbsp;<strong>rail&nbsp;network<\/strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;legendary&nbsp;for&nbsp;its&nbsp;affordability&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;long-distance&nbsp;sleeper&nbsp;trains&nbsp;cost&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$15<\/strong>.&nbsp;Local&nbsp;<strong>rickshaws<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;buses&nbsp;are&nbsp;equally&nbsp;cheap.&nbsp;Iconic&nbsp;attractions&nbsp;like&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Taj&nbsp;Mahal<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;temples&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Khajuraho<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>backwaters&nbsp;of&nbsp;Kerala<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;palaces&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Rajasthan<\/strong>&nbsp;make&nbsp;India&nbsp;a&nbsp;near-endless&nbsp;source&nbsp;of&nbsp;wonder.&nbsp;If&nbsp;you&#39;re&nbsp;from&nbsp;India&nbsp;and&nbsp;planning&nbsp;international&nbsp;trips&nbsp;on&nbsp;a&nbsp;budget,&nbsp;also&nbsp;check&nbsp;out&nbsp;our&nbsp;resource&nbsp;on&nbsp;Visa&nbsp;Free&nbsp;Countries&nbsp;For&nbsp;Indian&nbsp;Travelers.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>7.&nbsp;Nepal<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$20\u2013$35<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Nepal&nbsp;is&nbsp;a&nbsp;paradise&nbsp;for&nbsp;adventure&nbsp;travelers&nbsp;on&nbsp;a&nbsp;budget.&nbsp;<strong>Dal&nbsp;bhat<\/strong>&nbsp;(rice,&nbsp;lentils,&nbsp;and&nbsp;vegetables),&nbsp;the&nbsp;national&nbsp;dish,&nbsp;costs&nbsp;as&nbsp;little&nbsp;as&nbsp;<strong>$2\u2013$4<\/strong>&nbsp;at&nbsp;local&nbsp;teahouses&nbsp;and&nbsp;is&nbsp;often&nbsp;offered&nbsp;as&nbsp;an&nbsp;<strong>all-you-can-eat<\/strong>&nbsp;meal.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;guesthouses&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Kathmandu<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Pokhara<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;available&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$15&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;teahouse&nbsp;accommodation&nbsp;along&nbsp;popular&nbsp;trekking&nbsp;routes&nbsp;is&nbsp;similarly&nbsp;affordable.<\/p><p><\/p><p>Local&nbsp;<strong>buses&nbsp;and&nbsp;microvans<\/strong>&nbsp;connect&nbsp;major&nbsp;cities&nbsp;for&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$3\u2013$8<\/strong>.&nbsp;The&nbsp;real&nbsp;draw,&nbsp;of&nbsp;course,&nbsp;is&nbsp;<strong>trekking<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Annapurna&nbsp;Circuit<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Everest&nbsp;Base&nbsp;Camp<\/strong>&nbsp;trek&nbsp;are&nbsp;world-renowned&nbsp;experiences.&nbsp;<strong>Trekking&nbsp;permits<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;required&nbsp;but&nbsp;reasonably&nbsp;priced.&nbsp;Beyond&nbsp;the&nbsp;trails,&nbsp;<strong>Pashupatinath&nbsp;Temple<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;medieval&nbsp;city&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Bhaktapur<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;unmissable.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>8.&nbsp;Sri&nbsp;Lanka<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$30\u2013$50<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Sri&nbsp;Lanka&nbsp;punches&nbsp;well&nbsp;above&nbsp;its&nbsp;weight&nbsp;as&nbsp;a&nbsp;budget&nbsp;travel&nbsp;destination.&nbsp;Local&nbsp;<strong>rice&nbsp;and&nbsp;curry<\/strong>&nbsp;meals&nbsp;cost&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$2\u2013$4<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;fresh&nbsp;<strong>tropical&nbsp;fruit<\/strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;sold&nbsp;at&nbsp;roadside&nbsp;stalls&nbsp;for&nbsp;next&nbsp;to&nbsp;nothing.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;guesthouses&nbsp;are&nbsp;plentiful&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$25&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;while&nbsp;mid-range&nbsp;hotels&nbsp;hover&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$30\u2013$50<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p>The&nbsp;country&#39;s&nbsp;<strong>tuk-tuk<\/strong>&nbsp;network&nbsp;keeps&nbsp;local&nbsp;transport&nbsp;costs&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>$1\u2013$3<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;short&nbsp;trip,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>trains<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;particularly&nbsp;the&nbsp;famous&nbsp;<strong>Kandy&nbsp;to&nbsp;Ella<\/strong>&nbsp;scenic&nbsp;route&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;are&nbsp;both&nbsp;cheap&nbsp;and&nbsp;spectacular&nbsp;at&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$2\u2013$5<\/strong>.&nbsp;Highlights&nbsp;include&nbsp;the&nbsp;ancient&nbsp;ruins&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Sigiriya<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;colonial&nbsp;charm&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Galle&nbsp;Fort<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;tea&nbsp;plantations&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Nuwara&nbsp;Eliya<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;surf&nbsp;beaches&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Arugam&nbsp;Bay<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>9.&nbsp;Morocco<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$40\u2013$60<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Morocco&nbsp;offers&nbsp;a&nbsp;sensory&nbsp;overload&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;very&nbsp;reasonable&nbsp;price.&nbsp;<strong>Street&nbsp;food<\/strong>&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;famous&nbsp;<strong>Djemaa&nbsp;el-Fna<\/strong>&nbsp;square&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Marrakech<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;think&nbsp;<strong>harira&nbsp;soup<\/strong>,&nbsp;<strong>msemen<\/strong>&nbsp;(flatbread),&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>tagine<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;rarely&nbsp;costs&nbsp;more&nbsp;than&nbsp;<strong>$2\u2013$5<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;dish.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;<strong>riads<\/strong>&nbsp;(traditional&nbsp;guesthouses)&nbsp;and&nbsp;hostels&nbsp;are&nbsp;available&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$20&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;with&nbsp;accommodation&nbsp;covering&nbsp;$18&nbsp;per&nbsp;night&nbsp;on&nbsp;average&nbsp;for&nbsp;budget&nbsp;travelers.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>CTM&nbsp;buses<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>trains<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;cost-effective&nbsp;ways&nbsp;to&nbsp;travel&nbsp;between&nbsp;cities&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>Fez<\/strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Casablanca<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Chefchaouen<\/strong>,&nbsp;costing&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$15<\/strong>.&nbsp;The&nbsp;<strong>Sahara&nbsp;Desert<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;blue-painted&nbsp;streets&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Chefchaouen<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;ancient&nbsp;<strong>medina&nbsp;of&nbsp;Fez<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;experiences&nbsp;unlike&nbsp;anywhere&nbsp;else&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;world&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;and&nbsp;they&nbsp;cost&nbsp;very&nbsp;little&nbsp;to&nbsp;explore.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>10.&nbsp;Egypt<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$25\u2013$45<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Egypt&nbsp;is&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;historically&nbsp;rich&nbsp;yet&nbsp;<strong>affordable&nbsp;countries<\/strong>&nbsp;on&nbsp;earth.&nbsp;A&nbsp;hearty&nbsp;<strong>ful&nbsp;medames<\/strong>&nbsp;(fava&nbsp;bean&nbsp;stew)&nbsp;or&nbsp;a&nbsp;<strong>koshary<\/strong>&nbsp;(street&nbsp;food&nbsp;staple&nbsp;of&nbsp;rice,&nbsp;lentils,&nbsp;and&nbsp;pasta)&nbsp;will&nbsp;set&nbsp;you&nbsp;back&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$0.50\u2013$2<\/strong>.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;hotels&nbsp;and&nbsp;hostels&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Cairo<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Luxor<\/strong>&nbsp;start&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$8\u2013$20&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Minibuses<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>microvans<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;dirt-cheap&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>$0.20\u2013$1<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;ride.&nbsp;Felucca&nbsp;rides&nbsp;down&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Nile<\/strong>&nbsp;can&nbsp;be&nbsp;negotiated&nbsp;for&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$10<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;hour.&nbsp;The&nbsp;<strong>Pyramids&nbsp;of&nbsp;Giza<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;temples&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Luxor<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Karnak<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Valley&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;Kings<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;diving&nbsp;paradise&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Red&nbsp;Sea<\/strong>&nbsp;coast&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Dahab<\/strong>&nbsp;make&nbsp;Egypt&nbsp;a&nbsp;destination&nbsp;of&nbsp;near-mythical&nbsp;proportions&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;accessible&nbsp;on&nbsp;a&nbsp;shoestring&nbsp;budget.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>11.&nbsp;Turkey<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$35\u2013$55<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Turkey&#39;s&nbsp;combination&nbsp;of&nbsp;East-meets-West&nbsp;culture&nbsp;and&nbsp;relatively&nbsp;low&nbsp;prices&nbsp;makes&nbsp;it&nbsp;a&nbsp;top&nbsp;pick&nbsp;among&nbsp;budget&nbsp;travelers.&nbsp;A&nbsp;classic&nbsp;<strong>d\u00f6ner&nbsp;kebab<\/strong>&nbsp;or&nbsp;a&nbsp;plate&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>meze<\/strong>&nbsp;from&nbsp;a&nbsp;local&nbsp;restaurant&nbsp;costs&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$3\u2013$6<\/strong>.&nbsp;Hostels&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Istanbul<\/strong>&nbsp;start&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$15&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;with&nbsp;budget&nbsp;hotels&nbsp;available&nbsp;for&nbsp;<strong>$20\u2013$35<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p>Turkey&#39;s&nbsp;<strong>intercity&nbsp;buses<\/strong>&nbsp;(run&nbsp;by&nbsp;companies&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>Metro&nbsp;Turizm<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Kamil&nbsp;Ko\u00e7<\/strong>)&nbsp;are&nbsp;comfortable&nbsp;and&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$15<\/strong>&nbsp;between&nbsp;major&nbsp;cities.&nbsp;<strong>Istanbul&#39;s&nbsp;metro<\/strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;also&nbsp;excellent&nbsp;value&nbsp;at&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$0.50<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;ride.&nbsp;Unmissable&nbsp;sights&nbsp;include&nbsp;<strong>Hagia&nbsp;Sophia<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Grand&nbsp;Bazaar<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;surreal&nbsp;landscapes&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Cappadocia<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;turquoise&nbsp;coastline&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Turkish&nbsp;Riviera<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>12.&nbsp;Albania<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$30\u2013$50<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Albania&nbsp;is&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;Europe&#39;s&nbsp;best-kept&nbsp;budget&nbsp;secrets.&nbsp;<strong>Local&nbsp;food<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;grilled&nbsp;meats,&nbsp;<strong>byrek<\/strong>&nbsp;(savory&nbsp;pastry),&nbsp;and&nbsp;fresh&nbsp;seafood&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;is&nbsp;both&nbsp;delicious&nbsp;and&nbsp;cheap&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>$3\u2013$8<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;meal.&nbsp;Accommodation&nbsp;in&nbsp;cities&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>Tirana<\/strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Berat<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;coastal&nbsp;town&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Saranda<\/strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;widely&nbsp;available&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$15\u2013$30&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;with&nbsp;hostel&nbsp;beds&nbsp;starting&nbsp;from&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$8\u2013$12<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Minibuses&nbsp;(furgons)<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the&nbsp;primary&nbsp;form&nbsp;of&nbsp;intercity&nbsp;transport&nbsp;and&nbsp;cost&nbsp;<strong>$2\u2013$8<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;journey.&nbsp;Albania&#39;s&nbsp;<strong>Ionian&nbsp;coastline<\/strong>&nbsp;rivals&nbsp;anywhere&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;Mediterranean,&nbsp;the&nbsp;UNESCO-listed&nbsp;<strong>Old&nbsp;Town&nbsp;of&nbsp;Berat<\/strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;breathtaking,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Lake&nbsp;Koman<\/strong>&nbsp;offers&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;Europe&#39;s&nbsp;most&nbsp;stunning&nbsp;ferry&nbsp;rides&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;all&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;fraction&nbsp;of&nbsp;what&nbsp;you&#39;d&nbsp;pay&nbsp;in&nbsp;neighboring&nbsp;Greece&nbsp;or&nbsp;Italy.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>13.&nbsp;Georgia<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$35\u2013$60<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>The&nbsp;Republic&nbsp;of&nbsp;Georgia&nbsp;is&nbsp;a&nbsp;bargain&nbsp;across&nbsp;the&nbsp;board&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;from&nbsp;lodging&nbsp;to&nbsp;food&nbsp;to&nbsp;attractions.&nbsp;According&nbsp;to&nbsp;recent&nbsp;travel&nbsp;data,&nbsp;<strong>hotel&nbsp;rooms&nbsp;in&nbsp;Tbilisi<\/strong>&nbsp;start&nbsp;from&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$32&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;with&nbsp;hostel&nbsp;beds&nbsp;at&nbsp;Tbilisi&#39;s&nbsp;famous&nbsp;<strong>Fabrika&nbsp;Hostel<\/strong>&nbsp;available&nbsp;for&nbsp;as&nbsp;little&nbsp;as&nbsp;<strong>$9<\/strong>.&nbsp;Restaurant&nbsp;meals&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;glass&nbsp;of&nbsp;local&nbsp;wine&nbsp;cost&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$15<\/strong>,&nbsp;while&nbsp;a&nbsp;filling&nbsp;<strong>khachapuri<\/strong>&nbsp;(cheese&nbsp;bread)&nbsp;from&nbsp;a&nbsp;street&nbsp;vendor&nbsp;can&nbsp;be&nbsp;had&nbsp;for&nbsp;as&nbsp;little&nbsp;as&nbsp;<strong>$0.50\u2013$2<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p>The&nbsp;<strong>Tbilisi&nbsp;Metro<\/strong>&nbsp;costs&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$0.40&nbsp;per&nbsp;ride<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;long-distance&nbsp;buses&nbsp;to&nbsp;cities&nbsp;like&nbsp;<strong>Batumi<\/strong>&nbsp;run&nbsp;about&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$15<\/strong>&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;6-hour&nbsp;journey.&nbsp;Airport&nbsp;taxi&nbsp;transfers&nbsp;are&nbsp;under&nbsp;<strong>$15<\/strong>.&nbsp;Georgia&#39;s&nbsp;<strong>ancient&nbsp;monasteries<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;mountain&nbsp;town&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Kazbegi<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;world&#39;s&nbsp;oldest&nbsp;<strong>wine&nbsp;region<\/strong>&nbsp;in&nbsp;Kakheti&nbsp;are&nbsp;all&nbsp;extraordinary&nbsp;experiences.&nbsp;Skiing&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>Gudauri<\/strong>&nbsp;ski&nbsp;resort&nbsp;offers&nbsp;a&nbsp;full&nbsp;day&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;slopes&nbsp;for&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$27<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;a&nbsp;fraction&nbsp;of&nbsp;what&nbsp;you&#39;d&nbsp;pay&nbsp;in&nbsp;Western&nbsp;Europe&nbsp;or&nbsp;North&nbsp;America.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>14.&nbsp;Mexico<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$30\u2013$50<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Mexico&nbsp;is&nbsp;a&nbsp;<strong>budget&nbsp;travel&nbsp;guide<\/strong>&nbsp;staple&nbsp;for&nbsp;good&nbsp;reason.&nbsp;<strong>Street&nbsp;tacos<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;arguably&nbsp;the&nbsp;world&#39;s&nbsp;best&nbsp;street&nbsp;food&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;cost&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$0.50\u2013$2<\/strong>&nbsp;each,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>mercados<\/strong>&nbsp;(local&nbsp;markets)&nbsp;serve&nbsp;enormous,&nbsp;flavor-packed&nbsp;lunches&nbsp;for&nbsp;<strong>$3\u2013$5<\/strong>.&nbsp;Hostels&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Mexico&nbsp;City<\/strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Oaxaca<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Tulum<\/strong>&nbsp;start&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$8\u2013$15&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;with&nbsp;budget&nbsp;hotels&nbsp;available&nbsp;for&nbsp;<strong>$20\u2013$35<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Local&nbsp;buses<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;way&nbsp;to&nbsp;travel&nbsp;within&nbsp;cities&nbsp;at&nbsp;about&nbsp;<strong>$0.25\u2013$0.50<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;ride,&nbsp;while&nbsp;<strong>ADO&nbsp;buses<\/strong>&nbsp;connect&nbsp;major&nbsp;cities&nbsp;for&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$30<\/strong>.&nbsp;Top&nbsp;experiences&nbsp;include&nbsp;<strong>Chichen&nbsp;Itza<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;archaeological&nbsp;sites&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Teotihuacan<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;colorful&nbsp;streets&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Guanajuato<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;Caribbean&nbsp;beaches&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Yucat\u00e1n&nbsp;Peninsula<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>15.&nbsp;Bolivia<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$20\u2013$35<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Bolivia&nbsp;is&nbsp;consistently&nbsp;ranked&nbsp;as&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>cheapest&nbsp;countries&nbsp;to&nbsp;visit<\/strong>&nbsp;in&nbsp;all&nbsp;of&nbsp;South&nbsp;America.&nbsp;A&nbsp;<strong>set&nbsp;lunch&nbsp;menu<\/strong>&nbsp;(almuerzo)&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;local&nbsp;restaurant&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;typically&nbsp;including&nbsp;soup,&nbsp;a&nbsp;main&nbsp;course,&nbsp;and&nbsp;a&nbsp;drink&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;costs&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$1.50\u2013$3<\/strong>.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;accommodation&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>La&nbsp;Paz<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Sucre<\/strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;available&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$15&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Minibuses&nbsp;and&nbsp;shared&nbsp;taxis<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;extremely&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>$0.30\u2013$2<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;trip.&nbsp;The&nbsp;country&#39;s&nbsp;extraordinary&nbsp;landscapes&nbsp;include&nbsp;the&nbsp;otherworldly&nbsp;<strong>Salar&nbsp;de&nbsp;Uyuni<\/strong>&nbsp;(the&nbsp;world&#39;s&nbsp;largest&nbsp;salt&nbsp;flat),&nbsp;the&nbsp;dramatic&nbsp;<strong>Valle&nbsp;de&nbsp;la&nbsp;Luna<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;floating&nbsp;islands&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Lake&nbsp;Titicaca<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;lush&nbsp;<strong>Amazon&nbsp;Basin<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;all&nbsp;accessible&nbsp;on&nbsp;a&nbsp;backpacker&nbsp;budget.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>16.&nbsp;Peru<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$30\u2013$50<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Peru&nbsp;offers&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;rewarding&nbsp;travel&nbsp;experiences&nbsp;in&nbsp;South&nbsp;America&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;highly&nbsp;accessible&nbsp;price&nbsp;point.&nbsp;A&nbsp;<strong>comida&nbsp;corrida<\/strong>&nbsp;(set&nbsp;lunch)&nbsp;in&nbsp;a&nbsp;local&nbsp;restaurant&nbsp;costs&nbsp;<strong>$2\u2013$4<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;fresh&nbsp;<strong>ceviche<\/strong>&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;local&nbsp;market&nbsp;is&nbsp;surprisingly&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>$3\u2013$6<\/strong>.&nbsp;Hostels&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Cusco<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Lima<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;available&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$8\u2013$15&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Inca&nbsp;Rail&nbsp;and&nbsp;Peru&nbsp;Rail<\/strong>&nbsp;connect&nbsp;<strong>Cusco<\/strong>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<strong>Aguas&nbsp;Calientes<\/strong>&nbsp;(the&nbsp;gateway&nbsp;to&nbsp;<strong>Machu&nbsp;Picchu<\/strong>)&nbsp;for&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$30\u2013$80<\/strong>&nbsp;return,&nbsp;while&nbsp;local&nbsp;<strong>combis<\/strong>&nbsp;(minivans)&nbsp;are&nbsp;very&nbsp;cheap&nbsp;for&nbsp;city&nbsp;transport.&nbsp;The&nbsp;crown&nbsp;jewel&nbsp;is&nbsp;undoubtedly&nbsp;<strong>Machu&nbsp;Picchu<\/strong>,&nbsp;but&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Amazon&nbsp;rainforest<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Colca&nbsp;Canyon<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;colonial&nbsp;architecture&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Arequipa<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;equally&nbsp;compelling.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>17.&nbsp;Colombia<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$30\u2013$50<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Colombia&nbsp;has&nbsp;transformed&nbsp;into&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;South&nbsp;America&#39;s&nbsp;most&nbsp;exciting&nbsp;<strong>budget&nbsp;travel&nbsp;destinations<\/strong>.&nbsp;<strong>Set&nbsp;lunches&nbsp;(men\u00fa&nbsp;del&nbsp;d\u00eda)<\/strong>&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;a&nbsp;full&nbsp;meal&nbsp;with&nbsp;soup,&nbsp;main&nbsp;course,&nbsp;juice,&nbsp;and&nbsp;dessert&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;cost&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$3\u2013$5<\/strong>&nbsp;at&nbsp;local&nbsp;restaurants.&nbsp;Hostels&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Medell\u00edn<\/strong>,&nbsp;<strong>Bogot\u00e1<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Cartagena<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;available&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$8\u2013$15&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Metro&nbsp;and&nbsp;bus&nbsp;rapid&nbsp;transit&nbsp;(BRT)<\/strong>&nbsp;systems&nbsp;in&nbsp;Medell\u00edn&nbsp;and&nbsp;Bogot\u00e1&nbsp;are&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>$0.60\u2013$1<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;ride,&nbsp;while&nbsp;intercity&nbsp;<strong>long-distance&nbsp;buses<\/strong>&nbsp;cost&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$30<\/strong>.&nbsp;The&nbsp;walled&nbsp;colonial&nbsp;city&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Cartagena<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;vibrant&nbsp;street&nbsp;art&nbsp;scene&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Medell\u00edn<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;coffee&nbsp;farms&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Zona&nbsp;Cafetera<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;Amazon&nbsp;jungle&nbsp;near&nbsp;<strong>Leticia<\/strong>&nbsp;make&nbsp;Colombia&nbsp;a&nbsp;destination&nbsp;that&nbsp;rewards&nbsp;explorers&nbsp;at&nbsp;every&nbsp;price&nbsp;point.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>18.&nbsp;Portugal<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$50\u2013$70<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>As&nbsp;far&nbsp;as&nbsp;Western&nbsp;European&nbsp;destinations&nbsp;go,&nbsp;Portugal&nbsp;is&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;<strong>affordable&nbsp;countries&nbsp;to&nbsp;visit<\/strong>.&nbsp;A&nbsp;<strong>prato&nbsp;do&nbsp;dia<\/strong>&nbsp;(daily&nbsp;special)&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;local&nbsp;restaurant&nbsp;costs&nbsp;<strong>$8\u2013$12<\/strong>&nbsp;including&nbsp;wine,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>pastel&nbsp;de&nbsp;nata<\/strong>&nbsp;(custard&nbsp;tarts)&nbsp;from&nbsp;a&nbsp;bakery&nbsp;are&nbsp;just&nbsp;<strong>$1\u2013$2<\/strong>.&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;accommodation&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Lisbon<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Porto<\/strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;available&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$15\u2013$25&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>&nbsp;in&nbsp;hostels,&nbsp;with&nbsp;budget&nbsp;hotels&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$35\u2013$55<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Public&nbsp;transport<\/strong>&nbsp;in&nbsp;Lisbon&nbsp;and&nbsp;Porto&nbsp;is&nbsp;excellent&nbsp;and&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;at&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$1.50\u2013$2<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;journey,&nbsp;and&nbsp;regional&nbsp;trains&nbsp;connect&nbsp;cities&nbsp;for&nbsp;<strong>$15\u2013$30<\/strong>.&nbsp;Highlights&nbsp;include&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>historic&nbsp;districts&nbsp;of&nbsp;Alfama<\/strong>&nbsp;in&nbsp;Lisbon,&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Douro&nbsp;Valley&nbsp;wine&nbsp;region<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;dramatic&nbsp;cliffs&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>Algarve<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;UNESCO-listed&nbsp;<strong>city&nbsp;of&nbsp;Sintra<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>19.&nbsp;Croatia<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$55\u2013$80<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Croatia&nbsp;may&nbsp;be&nbsp;famous&nbsp;for&nbsp;its&nbsp;stunning&nbsp;<strong>Adriatic&nbsp;coastline<\/strong>,&nbsp;but&nbsp;it&nbsp;remains&nbsp;far&nbsp;more&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;than&nbsp;most&nbsp;other&nbsp;Mediterranean&nbsp;destinations.&nbsp;A&nbsp;<strong>meal&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;local&nbsp;konoba<\/strong>&nbsp;(tavern)&nbsp;costs&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$15<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>fresh&nbsp;seafood<\/strong>&nbsp;is&nbsp;widely&nbsp;available&nbsp;at&nbsp;reasonable&nbsp;prices.&nbsp;Hostels&nbsp;along&nbsp;the&nbsp;coast&nbsp;and&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Split<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Zagreb<\/strong>&nbsp;start&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$15\u2013$25&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;with&nbsp;budget&nbsp;hotels&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$40\u2013$60<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p><strong>Ferries<\/strong>&nbsp;between&nbsp;islands&nbsp;are&nbsp;run&nbsp;by&nbsp;<strong>Jadrolinija<\/strong>&nbsp;at&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$15<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;crossing,&nbsp;making&nbsp;island-hopping&nbsp;accessible.&nbsp;<strong>Split&#39;s&nbsp;historic&nbsp;old&nbsp;town<\/strong>&nbsp;(built&nbsp;around&nbsp;Diocletian&#39;s&nbsp;Palace),&nbsp;the&nbsp;walls&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Dubrovnik<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;waterfalls&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Plitvice&nbsp;Lakes&nbsp;National&nbsp;Park<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;islands&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Hvar<\/strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>Kor\u010dula<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;among&nbsp;Europe&#39;s&nbsp;most&nbsp;beautiful&nbsp;destinations&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;and&nbsp;Croatia&#39;s&nbsp;relative&nbsp;affordability&nbsp;keeps&nbsp;it&nbsp;within&nbsp;budget&nbsp;reach.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>20.&nbsp;Slovenia<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p><strong>Average&nbsp;Daily&nbsp;Budget:&nbsp;$50\u2013$75<\/strong><\/p><p><\/p><p>Small&nbsp;but&nbsp;spectacular,&nbsp;Slovenia&nbsp;is&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;Europe&#39;s&nbsp;most&nbsp;underrated&nbsp;and&nbsp;<strong>affordable&nbsp;countries<\/strong>.&nbsp;A&nbsp;meal&nbsp;at&nbsp;a&nbsp;local&nbsp;<strong>gostilna<\/strong>&nbsp;(traditional&nbsp;inn)&nbsp;costs&nbsp;<strong>$10\u2013$15<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;Slovenia&#39;s&nbsp;<strong>local&nbsp;wine&nbsp;and&nbsp;beer<\/strong>&nbsp;are&nbsp;excellent&nbsp;value&nbsp;at&nbsp;<strong>$2\u2013$4<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;glass.&nbsp;Hostels&nbsp;in&nbsp;<strong>Ljubljana<\/strong>&nbsp;start&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$15\u2013$20&nbsp;per&nbsp;night<\/strong>,&nbsp;with&nbsp;budget&nbsp;hotels&nbsp;from&nbsp;<strong>$35\u2013$55<\/strong>.<\/p><p><\/p><p>Ljubljana&#39;s&nbsp;efficient&nbsp;<strong>bus&nbsp;network<\/strong>&nbsp;operates&nbsp;at&nbsp;around&nbsp;<strong>$1.30<\/strong>&nbsp;per&nbsp;ride,&nbsp;and&nbsp;intercity&nbsp;buses&nbsp;connect&nbsp;major&nbsp;towns&nbsp;for&nbsp;<strong>$5\u2013$15<\/strong>.&nbsp;The&nbsp;iconic&nbsp;<strong>Lake&nbsp;Bled<\/strong>&nbsp;with&nbsp;its&nbsp;island&nbsp;church&nbsp;is&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;Europe&#39;s&nbsp;most&nbsp;photographed&nbsp;locations,&nbsp;while&nbsp;<strong>Triglav&nbsp;National&nbsp;Park<\/strong>,&nbsp;the&nbsp;<strong>So\u010da&nbsp;Valley<\/strong>,&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;underground&nbsp;caves&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong>Postojna<\/strong>&nbsp;round&nbsp;out&nbsp;a&nbsp;country&nbsp;that&nbsp;manages&nbsp;to&nbsp;pack&nbsp;enormous&nbsp;natural&nbsp;beauty&nbsp;into&nbsp;a&nbsp;very&nbsp;compact&nbsp;space.<\/p><p><\/p><h2><strong>Final&nbsp;Thoughts:&nbsp;Start&nbsp;Planning&nbsp;Your&nbsp;Budget&nbsp;Trip&nbsp;Today<\/strong><\/h2><p><\/p><p>From&nbsp;the&nbsp;rice&nbsp;paddies&nbsp;of&nbsp;Vietnam&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;salt&nbsp;flats&nbsp;of&nbsp;Bolivia,&nbsp;the&nbsp;world&#39;s&nbsp;most&nbsp;extraordinary&nbsp;destinations&nbsp;don&#39;t&nbsp;require&nbsp;a&nbsp;luxury&nbsp;travel&nbsp;budget.&nbsp;These&nbsp;<strong><u><a href=\"https:\/\/besttraveladvisory.com\/cheapest-countries-to-visit\/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">20&nbsp;cheapest&nbsp;countries&nbsp;to&nbsp;visit<\/a><\/u><\/strong>&nbsp;prove&nbsp;that&nbsp;with&nbsp;a&nbsp;little&nbsp;planning&nbsp;and&nbsp;the&nbsp;right&nbsp;information,&nbsp;you&nbsp;can&nbsp;experience&nbsp;breathtaking&nbsp;cultures,&nbsp;stunning&nbsp;landscapes,&nbsp;and&nbsp;unforgettable&nbsp;adventures&nbsp;without&nbsp;financial&nbsp;stress.<\/p><p><\/p><p>The&nbsp;key&nbsp;is&nbsp;research,&nbsp;flexibility,&nbsp;and&nbsp;knowing&nbsp;where&nbsp;to&nbsp;look.&nbsp;Start&nbsp;by&nbsp;identifying&nbsp;which&nbsp;region&nbsp;calls&nbsp;to&nbsp;you&nbsp;most,&nbsp;set&nbsp;a&nbsp;realistic&nbsp;daily&nbsp;budget&nbsp;using&nbsp;the&nbsp;figures&nbsp;above&nbsp;as&nbsp;your&nbsp;guide,&nbsp;and&nbsp;begin&nbsp;mapping&nbsp;out&nbsp;your&nbsp;itinerary.&nbsp;For&nbsp;travelers&nbsp;looking&nbsp;to&nbsp;experience&nbsp;the&nbsp;world&nbsp;at&nbsp;the&nbsp;absolute&nbsp;cutting&nbsp;edge&nbsp;of&nbsp;luxury&nbsp;before&nbsp;diving&nbsp;into&nbsp;budget&nbsp;adventures,&nbsp;it&#39;s&nbsp;also&nbsp;worth&nbsp;knowing&nbsp;what&#39;s&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;opposite&nbsp;end&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;spectrum&nbsp;\u2014&nbsp;explore&nbsp;our&nbsp;feature&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;[World&#39;s&nbsp;Most&nbsp;Expensive&nbsp;Hotels]&nbsp;to&nbsp;see&nbsp;just&nbsp;how&nbsp;far&nbsp;the&nbsp;spectrum&nbsp;stretches.<\/p><p><\/p><p>Your&nbsp;next&nbsp;adventure&nbsp;is&nbsp;far&nbsp;more&nbsp;affordable&nbsp;than&nbsp;you&nbsp;think.&nbsp;Pick&nbsp;a&nbsp;destination,&nbsp;pack&nbsp;your&nbsp;bags,&nbsp;and&nbsp;get&nbsp;moving.<\/p>","excerpt":"","featuredImage":"https:\/\/api.blog-panel.clickstar.pl\/uploads\/blogs\/1791094213735-62eb841a-9565-46a2-b421-6d1edba5ddb1.png","featuredImageAlt":"Cheapest Countries to Visit","images":[],"tags":[],"categoryId":{"_id":"6abfc26801767108a4450264","name":"Budget Travel","slug":"budget-travel","status":"active"},"authorName":"Admin","publishDate":"2026-10-04T00:00:00.000Z","focusKeyword":"Cheapest Countries to Visit","secondaryKeywords":[],"metaTitle":"20 Cheapest Countries to Visit for Budget Travelers","metaDescription":"Discover the 20 cheapest countries to visit with affordable food, hotels, transport, and attractions for an unforgettable budget-friendly trip.\n","metaKeyword":"","canonicalUrl":"","ogTitle":"20 Cheapest Countries to Visit for Budget Travelers","ogDescription":